        "content" : {
          "size" : 9393,
          "compression" : 0,
          "mimeType" : "text/html; charset=utf-8",
          "text" : "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<!--LAB_HEAD_START-->\n    <head>\n        <link href=/resources/labheader/css/academyLabHeader.css rel=stylesheet>\n        <link href=/resources/css/labsBlog.css rel=stylesheet>\n        <title>Weak isolation on dual-use endpoint</title>\n    </head>\n<!--LAB_HEAD_END-->\n    <body>\n        <script src=\"/resources/labheader/js/labHeader.js\"></script>\n        <!--LAB_HEADER_START-->\n        <div id=\"academyLabHeader\">\n            <section class='academyLabBanner'>\n                <div class=container>\n                    <div class=logo></div>\n                        <div class=title-container>\n                            <h2>Weak isolation on dual-use endpoint</h2>\n                            <a class=link-back href='https://portswigger.net/web-security/logic-flaws/examples/lab-logic-flaws-weak-isolation-on-dual-use-endpoint'>\n                                Back&nbsp;to&nbsp;lab&nbsp;description&nbsp;\n                                <svg version=1.1 id=Layer_1 xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' xmlns:xlink='http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink' x=0px y=0px viewBox='0 0 28 30' enable-background='new 0 0 28 30' xml:space=preserve title=back-arrow>\n                                    <g>\n                                        <polygon points='1.4,0 0,1.2 12.6,15 0,28.8 1.4,30 15.1,15'></polygon>\n                                        <polygon points='14.3,0 12.9,1.2 25.6,15 12.9,28.8 14.3,30 28,15'></polygon>\n                                    </g>\n                                </svg>\n                            </a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class='widgetcontainer-lab-status is-notsolved'>\n                            <span>LAB</span>\n                            <p>Not solved</p>\n                            <span class=lab-status-icon></span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n        <!--LAB_HEADER_END-->\n        <div theme=\"blog\">\n            <section class=\"maincontainer\">\n                <div class=\"container is-page\">\n                    <header class=\"navigation-header\">\n                        <section class=\"top-links\">\n                            <a href=/>Home</a><p>|</p>\n                            <a href=\"/my-account?id=wiener\">My account</a><p>|</p>\n                        </section>\n                    </header>\n                    <header class=\"notification-header\">\n                    </header>\n                    <div class=\"blog-post\">\n                    <img src=\"/image/blog/posts/46.jpg\">\n                    <h1>Stag Do&apos;s</h1>\n                    <p><span id=blog-author>Paige Turner</span> | 02 February 2026</p>\n                    <hr>\n                    <p>Whenever a friend or relative announces their engagement, there is always one burning question that isn&apos;t really asked straight away out of politeness for the bride to be. While you&apos;re stood their feigning interest and enthusiasm for yet another wedding to cough up for, what you&apos;re really thinking is &apos;where&apos;s the stag do?&apos;.</p>\n                    <p>I couldn&apos;t possibly comment on the mentality of women when it comes to hen parties, but I&apos;ve seen enough phallic shaped balloons and cowgirl hats to make me think they get equally as excited at the prospect of going out for the weekend and getting the hen absolutely merry.</p>\n                    <p>When it comes to stags though, certainly you await the fateful news with excitement and dread. The destination also weighs heavily on the mentality of the best man. If your best man is likely to be someone with a nickname like &apos;Smudger or anything ending with the word &apos;dog&apos;, you can bet your bottom dollar that it&apos;s about to be a very wild adventure and an unpleasant one for the stag. In this day and age it&apos;s more likely to be a destination further afield and awaiting the news is sort of like a much bigger anxiety inducing gender reveal at a baby shower.</p>\n                    <p>Some of the big hitters are Vegas, Amsterdam, Prague, London and New York. It really is the chance to put other cultures off of yours within an impressively short two, maybe three evenings. Whoever thought up shots was clearly an evil genius. What do you need when drinking alcohol? Well, more concentrated alcohol obviously. How do you spot the groom from the crowd? Well, he&apos;s the one dressed as a baby or some sort of cowboy / crossdresser. Another useful tool is to check which man is being roundly screwed over with shot amounts and forfeits.</p>\n                    <p>The stag do is now a huge industry, with companies being set up all the time to answer the prayers of young men and deliver them some outlandish activities. Speaking of which, when the modern stag was being planned, someone had the good idea to say &apos;you know what? Maybe we should break up the drinking with some sort of activity!&apos;. And from this, all manner of garbage was introduced. Go Karting in Bruges? Why check out the scenery of somewhere brand new when you can do some run of the mill activity and pay for pleasure of flights and accommodation too. Next stag, ten pin bowling in Amsterdam. Whoever set up these companies to charge men an obscene amount of money to do something you can do five minutes from home in another country are cashing in big time.</p>\n                    <p>Ultimately, we do it for the groom to be. However, their face on arrival at the airport says is all. &apos;Why oh why have I done this? Maybe I shouldn&apos;t get married after all.&apos; But it&apos;s all worth it in the end when you return home, hungover, broke and having to keep some heavy secrets at the wedding right? Right?</p>\n                    <div/>\n                    <hr>\n                    <h1>Comments</h1>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Nick O&apos;Time | 02 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>I have nothing to say about this I&apos;m just typing until the creepy guy in the caf&apos; goes away.</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Jin Galbells | 11 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>I normally love to argue with everything I read online but I find it hard to be outraged by this.</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Andy Man | 13 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>I want to make something clear. My screen. It&apos;s beyond dusty.</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Peg Up | 14 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>How do I start my own blog?</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Paige Turner | 16 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>Amusing, enticing and well put together. But enough from my dating profile, good blog</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <hr>\n                    <section class=\"add-comment\">\n                        <h2>Leave a comment</h2>\n                        <form action=\"/post/comment\" method=\"POST\" enctype=\"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\">\n                            <input required type=\"hidden\" name=\"csrf\" value=\"i9BH14Aph6TLy47meS5sTg1JkbygX67e\">\n                            <input required type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value=\"4\">\n                            <label>Comment:</label>\n                            <textarea required rows=\"12\" cols=\"300\" name=\"comment\"></textarea>\n                                    <label>Name:</label>\n                                    <input required type=\"text\" name=\"name\">\n                                    <label>Email:</label>\n                                    <input required type=\"email\" name=\"email\">\n                                    <label>Website:</label>\n                                    <input pattern=\"(http:|https:).+\" type=\"text\" name=\"website\">\n                            <button class=\"button\" type=\"submit\">Post Comment</button>\n                        </form>\n                    </section>\n                    <div class=\"is-linkback\">\n                        <a href=\"/\">Back to Blog</a>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n            <div class=\"footer-wrapper\">\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </body>\n</html>\n"
